    <p class="title is-5 mathjax">
      
        ASAP: <span class="search-hit mathjax">Attention</span> Sink Anchored Pruning
      
    </p>
    <p class="authors">
      <span class="has-text-black-bis has-text-weight-semibold">Authors:</span>
      
      <a href="/search/?searchtype=author&amp;query=Lee%2C+J">Jaehyuk Lee</a>, 
      
      <a href="/search/?searchtype=author&amp;query=Kim%2C+H">Hanyoung Kim</a>, 
      
      <a href="/search/?searchtype=author&amp;query=Kim%2C+Y">Yanggee Kim</a>, 
      
      <a href="/search/?searchtype=author&amp;query=Lee%2C+D">Donghun Lee</a>
      
    </p>
    
    <p class="abstract mathjax">
      <span class="has-text-black-bis has-text-weight-semibold">Abstract</span>:
      <span class="abstract-short has-text-grey-dark mathjax" id="2605.22372v2-abstract-short" style="display: inline;">
        Vision Transformers (ViTs) face severe computational bottlenecks due to the quadratic complexity of self-<span class="search-hit mathjax">attention</span> at high resolutions. Existing token reduction methods rely on local metrics -- such as single-layer&hellip;
        <a class="is-size-7" style="white-space: nowrap;" onclick="document.getElementById('2605.22372v2-abstract-full').style.display = 'inline'; document.getElementById('2605.22372v2-abstract-short').style.display = 'none';">&#9661; More</a>
      </span>
      <span class="abstract-full has-text-grey-dark mathjax" id="2605.22372v2-abstract-full" style="display: none;">
        Vision Transformers (ViTs) face severe computational bottlenecks due to the quadratic complexity of self-<span class="search-hit mathjax">attention</span> at high resolutions. Existing token reduction methods rely on local metrics -- such as single-layer <span class="search-hit mathjax">attention</span> scores -- that are inherently vulnerable to the <span class="search-hit mathjax">attention</span> sink phenomenon, where uninformative tokens are paradoxically preserved over salient foreground objects. We propose ASAP (<span class="search-hit mathjax">Attention</span> Sink Anchored Pruning), a training-free framework that recasts this sink as a feature. Modeling ViT <span class="search-hit mathjax">information</span> <span class="search-hit mathjax">flow</span> as a Lazy Random Walk, ASAP identifies the sink as a dominant accumulator of probability mass. By computing the diffusion distance to the sink within the cumulative transition matrix, ASAP partitions tokens via Radial Diffusion Clustering and compresses background redundancy through Transition Weight Pooling in a single shot. Extensive experiments across image, video, and vision-<span class="search-hit mathjax">language</span> tasks demonstrate ASAP outperforms state-of-the-art methods, accelerating throughput by up to 48% while maintaining or even exceeding baseline accuracy.
        <a class="is-size-7" style="white-space: nowrap;" onclick="document.getElementById('2605.22372v2-abstract-full').style.display = 'none'; document.getElementById('2605.22372v2-abstract-short').style.display = 'inline';">&#9651; Less</a>
      </span>
    </p>
    

    <p class="is-size-7"><span class="has-text-black-bis has-text-weight-semibold">Submitted</span> 5 November, 2026; <span class="has-text-black-bis has-text-weight-semibold">v1</span> submitted 21 May, 2026;
      <span class="has-text-black-bis has-text-weight-semibold">originally announced</span> May 2026.
      
    </p>
    
    <p class="comments is-size-7">
      <span class="has-text-black-bis has-text-weight-semibold">Comments:</span>
      <span class="has-text-grey-dark mathjax">Accepted to NeurIPS 2026</span>
    </p>
    

    

    
